{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_21-49-09-omnipaxos-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor i in s['interpretations']:\n    if i.get('id','').startswith('802459cad83047a0aa0bbbd9f41a7cdc'):\n        print(json.dumps({k:i[k] for k in ('conclusion','defect_claim','counterevidence','limitations','joint_history') if k in i}, indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The entry-point documentation promises only that the future resolves when the assigned log index is decided, and advises re-reading the returned index only for `Superseded`; read that way `Ok(idx)` claims nothing about the value at `idx`. That is weaker than what the example and the two asserting test scenarios expect, which is why the finding rests on those expectations rather than on the wording alone.\",\n  \"A new leader must adopt any value a majority-overlapping write quorum already accepted, so an entry that reached a write quorum cannot be replaced; both mechanisms therefore need the assignment to be local-only or the entries to be discarded, which the receipts support (origin decided index 0 in the violating runs, the new leader's decided values excluding the origin's entries).\",\n  \"No retained run exhibits the two mechanisms together in one call, nor a re-synchronisation that both completes and carries decided progress while the origin's entries are discarded, so the intermediate steps of the second mechanism remain unobserved even though its endpoints are complete and reproduced.\",\n  \"The placeholder queue is unobservable through the public API, so its accounting is the explanation the endpoints imply rather than a direct measurement; the flush-deferral and accept-sync rules behind the condition are source-derived and consistent with the phase fields of the runs.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"Six retained configurations, all with batch_size 3 at the origin, a three-node cluster, majority quorum, a leader origin and an in-process in-memory transport; follower origins, other batch sizes, flexible quorums and crash recovery are unmeasured.\",\n  \"The boundary between the correct and shifted outcomes is bracketed rather than located (250 vs 500 ms ticks, and the flush deadline varied only at 100 and 1000 ms).\",\n  \"Both mechanisms are established for this snapshot's build with the default features through the actor layer's public handle; nothing here extends to other revisions of the crate, and the repository's own test scenarios that assert the value at the returned index were not executed here, so whether they pass or fail under these configurations is unknown.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"One fixed experiment and its successive revisions on one construction: the original three-case probe, the tick-period sweep, the revision adding the origin's promise and phase measurements, the revision parameterising the follower's flush deadline, and the revision parameterising it for the parameterised case as well. Scenario steps, batch size, election and resend tick counts and the measured quantities are unchanged across them; only the tick period, the flush deadline, the poll flag and read-only measurements differ, so the six configurations read as one comparison.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
